Description: read-only security audit for Linux with a 1-10 score
 linaudit checks a Linux system for common security problems and gives it a
 score from 1 (worst) to 10 (best), together with the findings sorted by
 severity and how to fix each one.
 .
 It runs more than 100 checks in nine categories: accounts and sudo, SSH,
 filesystem permissions, plaintext secrets, network and firewall, patching,
 persistence and signs of compromise, kernel and service hardening, and
 common server applications (Tomcat, Redis, Docker, PostgreSQL, Samba,
 Apache, nginx).
 .
 It never modifies the system and never prints the value of a secret, only
 where it was found. Profiles adapt the criteria to servers, desktops and
 containers. Reports are shown in an interactive terminal interface, as
 text, or as JSON for a central collector. Available in English and Spanish.
